Values are at most 1e5, so I use two Fenwick trees indexed by value: one for counts and one for sums. I also keep a queue of the last m elements.

**Adding an element.** Append `num` to the queue and update both trees. If the queue now holds more than m elements, remove the oldest one from both trees.

**Calculating the average.** If fewer than m elements have been seen, return -1. Otherwise the container holds exactly m elements. I need the sum of the elements ranked k+1 through m-k in sorted order, which equals `prefixSum(m-k smallest) - prefixSum(k smallest)`.

**Sum of the t smallest elements.**
1. Descend the count Fenwick tree to find the largest position `pos` whose prefix count is less than t. Accumulate the count and the sum along the way.
2. The value `pos+1` then covers the remaining `t - cnt` elements, so the result is `sum + (t - cnt) * (pos+1)`.

The descent uses LOG = 17, since 2^17 = 131072 > 1e5, and the tree size N is 100001 (any power of two at least that large works for the bounds check).

The descent runs like this:
```
pos=0; for i=LOG down to 0: np=pos+(1<<i); if np<=N and cnt[np]<t(remaining): pos=np; remaining-=cnt[np]; sum+=sm[np]
```
Using `remaining = t`, the loop condition is `cnt[np] < remaining`. At the end, the sum is `sum + remaining*(pos+1)`.

The answer is `intdiv(total, m-2k)`. All sums are positive, so integer division rounds down correctly. PHP integers are 64-bit, so there is no overflow.

```php
class MKAverage {
    private $m, $k, $N, $cnt, $sm, $q, $head, $tail;

    function __construct($m, $k) {
        $this->m = $m;
        $this->k = $k;
        $this->N = 100001;
        $this->cnt = array_fill(0, $this->N + 1, 0);
        $this->sm = array_fill(0, $this->N + 1, 0);
        $this->q = [];
        $this->head = 0;
    }

    private function upd($v, $dc) {
        $ds = $dc * $v;
        for ($i = $v; $i <= $this->N; $i += $i & -$i) {
            $this->cnt[$i] += $dc;
            $this->sm[$i] += $ds;
        }
    }

    private function smallest($t) {
        $pos = 0;
        $sum = 0;
        $rem = $t;
        for ($i = 17; $i >= 0; $i--) {
            $np = $pos + (1 << $i);
            if ($np <= $this->N && $this->cnt[$np] < $rem) {
                $pos = $np;
                $rem -= $this->cnt[$np];
                $sum += $this->sm[$np];
            }
        }
        return $sum + $rem * ($pos + 1);
    }

    function addElement($num) {
        $this->q[] = $num;
        $this->upd($num, 1);
        if (count($this->q) - $this->head > $this->m) {
            $old = $this->q[$this->head];
            unset($this->q[$this->head]);
            $this->head++;
            $this->upd($old, -1);
        }
    }

    function calculateMKAverage() {
        if (count($this->q) - $this->head < $this->m) return -1;
        $total = $this->smallest($this->m - $this->k) - $this->smallest($this->k);
        return intdiv($total, $this->m - 2 * $this->k);
    }
}
```

