This is a bitmask DP over which elements have already been used.

Let `dp[mask]` be the best score obtainable once the elements in `mask` have been removed. The number of operations already done is `popcount(mask) / 2`, so the next operation has index `popcount(mask) / 2 + 1`.

1. Precompute `gcd` for every pair `(i, j)`.
2. Start with `dp[0] = 0` and every other state at `-1` (unreachable).
3. For each reachable `mask` with an even popcount, pick the lowest unset bit `i`. Pairing the lowest unset element first is enough, since every element must be paired eventually. Then try every `j > i` that is not in `mask`.
4. Update `dp[mask | (1<<i) | (1<<j)]` with `dp[mask] + k * g[i][j]`, where `k = popcount(mask)/2 + 1`.
5. The answer is `dp[(1<<m) - 1]`.

There are at most 2^14 = 16384 masks and about 14 pairs per mask, so this is fast. Popcount is computed incrementally with `pc[mask] = pc[mask >> 1] + (mask & 1)`.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param Integer[] $nums
     * @return Integer
     */
    function maxScore($nums) {
        $m = count($nums);
        $g = [];
        for ($i = 0; $i < $m; $i++) {
            for ($j = $i + 1; $j < $m; $j++) {
                $a = $nums[$i];
                $b = $nums[$j];
                while ($b) {
                    $t = $a % $b;
                    $a = $b;
                    $b = $t;
                }
                $g[$i][$j] = $a;
            }
        }
        $full = (1 << $m) - 1;
        $dp = array_fill(0, $full + 1, -1);
        $pc = array_fill(0, $full + 1, 0);
        for ($mask = 1; $mask <= $full; $mask++) {
            $pc[$mask] = $pc[$mask >> 1] + ($mask & 1);
        }
        $dp[0] = 0;
        for ($mask = 0; $mask < $full; $mask++) {
            if ($dp[$mask] < 0) continue;
            $k = intdiv($pc[$mask], 2) + 1;
            $i = 0;
            while ($mask & (1 << $i)) $i++;
            for ($j = $i + 1; $j < $m; $j++) {
                if ($mask & (1 << $j)) continue;
                $nm = $mask | (1 << $i) | (1 << $j);
                $v = $dp[$mask] + $k * $g[$i][$j];
                if ($v > $dp[$nm]) $dp[$nm] = $v;
            }
        }
        return $dp[$full];
    }
}
```

