The minimum number of operations equals the sum of the prime factors of n, counted with multiplicity. For n = 1 this sum is 0.

To compute it, divide n by each factor d starting at 2. While d divides n, add d to the answer and divide n by d. Then move to the next d. Any remainder greater than 1 is itself prime, so add it to the answer.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param Integer $n
     * @return Integer
     */
    function minSteps($n) {
        $res = 0;
        for ($d = 2; $d * $d <= $n; $d++) {
            while ($n % $d == 0) {
                $res += $d;
                $n = intdiv($n, $d);
            }
        }
        if ($n > 1) {
            $res += $n;
        }
        return $res;
    }
}
```

