- Sort `arr` and build a map from value to dp.
- For each i, loop j from 0 to i-1 and take a = arr[j]. If a·a > x, we could break, but a plain loop of O(n²) is fine for n = 1000.
- Check `x % a == 0` and `isset(map[x/a])`. Use `intdiv` to keep integer types.
- Accumulate dp[x] = (dp[x] + dp[a]·dp[b]) % mod.

Both orderings (a, b) and (b, a) are counted automatically, because j iterates over every smaller element, so a and b each take a turn as the left child. When a = b, it is counted once, which is correct.

