The maximum OR is the OR of all elements, since OR only ever adds bits. With at most 16 elements, a DFS over include/exclude choices visits at most 2^16 subsets, which is fast enough. At the end of each branch, count it if its OR equals the maximum. Every element is at least 1, so the empty subset has OR 0, which never equals the maximum and is never counted.

```php
class Solution {
    private $n;
    private $nums;
    private $target;

    /**
     * @param Integer[] $nums
     * @return Integer
     */
    function countMaxOrSubsets($nums) {
        $this->nums = $nums;
        $this->n = count($nums);
        $t = 0;
        foreach ($nums as $x) $t |= $x;
        $this->target = $t;
        return $this->dfs(0, 0);
    }

    private function dfs($i, $cur) {
        if ($i == $this->n) {
            return $cur == $this->target ? 1 : 0;
        }
        return $this->dfs($i + 1, $cur | $this->nums[$i]) + $this->dfs($i + 1, $cur);
    }
}
```

