Since n is at most 250, a brute force over every pair (a, b) is fast enough. For each pair, compute a² + b², take the integer square root c, and count the pair if c² equals the sum and c ≤ n. Ordered pairs are counted separately, so (3,4,5) and (4,3,5) each contribute one, matching the examples.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param Integer $n
     * @return Integer
     */
    function countTriples($n) {
        $count = 0;
        for ($a = 1; $a <= $n; $a++) {
            for ($b = 1; $b <= $n; $b++) {
                $s = $a * $a + $b * $b;
                $c = (int)round(sqrt($s));
                if ($c <= $n && $c * $c == $s) {
                    $count++;
                }
            }
        }
        return $count;
    }
}
```

