Remove all dashes, uppercase the rest, then insert dashes so every group has exactly `k` characters except possibly the first.

Steps:
1. Strip dashes with `str_replace` and convert to uppercase with `strtoupper`.
2. Let `n` be the length of the cleaned string. If `n` is 0, return an empty string.
3. The first group has length `n % k`, or `k` if that remainder is 0.
4. Take the first group, then append each following block of `k` characters, joining the groups with dashes.

The examples show a trailing space in the string, as in "5F3Z-2e-9-w ". This is most likely a formatting artifact. If the space were really part of the input, it would be treated as a character and kept. I'll treat it as an artifact and apply the standard solution.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param String $s
     * @param Integer $k
     * @return String
     */
    function licenseKeyFormatting($s, $k) {
        $t = strtoupper(str_replace('-', '', $s));
        $n = strlen($t);
        if ($n == 0) return "";
        $first = $n % $k;
        if ($first == 0) $first = $k;
        $parts = [substr($t, 0, $first)];
        for ($i = $first; $i < $n; $i += $k) {
            $parts[] = substr($t, $i, $k);
        }
        return implode('-', $parts);
    }
}
```

