For each point i, count how many other points share each normalized slope from i, and take the largest count plus one. Since all points are unique, there are no duplicate points to handle.

To normalize a slope, take dx and dy, divide both by gcd(|dx|, |dy|), and fix the sign so that dx > 0, or dx == 0 and dy > 0. Then use the string "dx,dy" as the hash key.

If n <= 2, return n.

The gcd is a simple Euclidean loop. With dx == 0, gcd(0, |dy|) = |dy|, so the key becomes "0,1", which is fine. The same holds for dy == 0, which gives "1,0".

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param Integer[][] $points
     * @return Integer
     */
    function maxPoints($points) {
        $n = count($points);
        if ($n <= 2) return $n;
        $best = 1;
        for ($i = 0; $i < $n; $i++) {
            $map = [];
            $local = 0;
            for ($j = $i + 1; $j < $n; $j++) {
                $dx = $points[$j][0] - $points[$i][0];
                $dy = $points[$j][1] - $points[$i][1];
                $a = abs($dx);
                $b = abs($dy);
                while ($b != 0) {
                    $t = $a % $b;
                    $a = $b;
                    $b = $t;
                }
                if ($a != 0) {
                    $dx = intdiv($dx, $a);
                    $dy = intdiv($dy, $a);
                }
                if ($dx < 0 || ($dx == 0 && $dy < 0)) {
                    $dx = -$dx;
                    $dy = -$dy;
                }
                $key = $dx . "," . $dy;
                if (!isset($map[$key])) $map[$key] = 0;
                $map[$key]++;
                if ($map[$key] > $local) $local = $map[$key];
            }
            if ($local + 1 > $best) $best = $local + 1;
        }
        return $best;
    }
}
```

