Since m ≤ 8, a bitmask DP over mentors works.

1. Precompute `score[i][j]`, the number of matching answers between student `i` and mentor `j`.
2. Let `dp[mask]` be the best total score when the mentors in `mask` are already assigned to the first `popcount(mask)` students.
3. For each mask, the next student is `i = popcount(mask)`. For each mentor `j` not in the mask, update `dp[mask | (1<<j)] = max(dp[mask | (1<<j)], dp[mask] + score[i][j])`.
4. The answer is `dp[(1<<m) - 1]`.

Initialise `dp` to -1 (unreachable) with `dp[0] = 0`. The popcount is computed by a simple loop over the bits.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param Integer[][] $students
     * @param Integer[][] $mentors
     * @return Integer
     */
    function maxCompatibilitySum($students, $mentors) {
        $m = count($students);
        $n = count($students[0]);
        $score = [];
        for ($i = 0; $i < $m; $i++) {
            for ($j = 0; $j < $m; $j++) {
                $s = 0;
                for ($k = 0; $k < $n; $k++) {
                    if ($students[$i][$k] == $mentors[$j][$k]) $s++;
                }
                $score[$i][$j] = $s;
            }
        }
        $full = (1 << $m) - 1;
        $dp = array_fill(0, $full + 1, -1);
        $dp[0] = 0;
        for ($mask = 0; $mask < $full; $mask++) {
            if ($dp[$mask] < 0) continue;
            $i = 0;
            for ($b = 0; $b < $m; $b++) {
                if ($mask & (1 << $b)) $i++;
            }
            for ($j = 0; $j < $m; $j++) {
                if (!($mask & (1 << $j))) {
                    $nm = $mask | (1 << $j);
                    $v = $dp[$mask] + $score[$i][$j];
                    if ($v > $dp[$nm]) $dp[$nm] = $v;
                }
            }
        }
        return $dp[$full];
    }
}
```

