This is a row-by-row bitmask DP.

For each row, compute `avail`, the bitmask of good seats. A mask is valid for a row if it is a subset of `avail` and has no two adjacent bits, i.e. `(mask & (mask >> 1)) == 0`.

Let `dp[mask]` be the best total after the current row when that row uses `mask`. A transition from a previous mask `p` to a current mask `c` is allowed when `(c & (p << 1)) == 0` and `(c & (p >> 1)) == 0`. This blocks the upper-left and upper-right neighbours.

The previous row starts as `dp = [0 => 0]`, which is the empty mask. After the last row, the answer is the maximum value in `dp`.

Seat characters might carry trailing spaces, as in the examples' formatting, so I only test whether a cell equals `'.'`, using `trim` to be safe. Broken seats are `'#'`, so a cell counts as good only if its trimmed value is `'.'`. Example 3 shows `**.**`, which is just markdown formatting, so I also treat any cell containing `.` as good. Checking `strpos($cell, '#') === false` would be wrong if a cell were empty, so I check for `.` directly with `strpos($c, '.') !== false`.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param String[][] $seats
     * @return Integer
     */
    function maxStudents($seats) {
        $m = count($seats);
        $n = count($seats[0]);
        $dp = [0 => 0];
        for ($i = 0; $i < $m; $i++) {
            $avail = 0;
            for ($j = 0; $j < $n; $j++) {
                $c = (string)$seats[$i][$j];
                if (strpos($c, '.') !== false) {
                    $avail |= (1 << $j);
                }
            }
            $ndp = [];
            for ($c = 0; $c < (1 << $n); $c++) {
                if (($c & $avail) != $c) continue;
                if (($c & ($c >> 1)) != 0) continue;
                $cnt = 0;
                $t = $c;
                while ($t) {
                    $cnt += $t & 1;
                    $t >>= 1;
                }
                $best = -1;
                foreach ($dp as $p => $v) {
                    if (($c & ($p << 1)) == 0 && ($c & ($p >> 1)) == 0) {
                        if ($v > $best) $best = $v;
                    }
                }
                if ($best >= 0) {
                    $ndp[$c] = $best + $cnt;
                }
            }
            $dp = $ndp;
        }
        return max($dp);
    }
}
```

