Use DP over time: `dp[t][v]` is the minimum cost to be at city `v` at exactly time `t`.

- Base case: `dp[0][0] = passingFees[0]`.
- Transition: for each `t` from 1 to `maxTime` and each edge `(u, v, w)` with `w <= t`, set `dp[t][v] = min(dp[t][v], dp[t-w][u] + fee[v])`, and symmetrically for `u`.
- Answer: the minimum of `dp[t][n-1]` over all `t <= maxTime`, or -1 if none is reachable.

Since every `w >= 1`, each state depends only on strictly smaller times, so the order of computation is safe.

Complexity is `maxTime * edges * 2`, about 2M operations, which is fine.

Memory: 1001 × 1000 entries is about 1M, which is acceptable in PHP. To reduce it, I store each time layer as a plain array filled with INF.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param Integer $maxTime
     * @param Integer[][] $edges
     * @param Integer[] $passingFees
     * @return Integer
     */
    function minCost($maxTime, $edges, $passingFees) {
        $n = count($passingFees);
        $INF = PHP_INT_MAX;
        $dp = [];
        for ($t = 0; $t <= $maxTime; $t++) {
            $dp[$t] = array_fill(0, $n, $INF);
        }
        $dp[0][0] = $passingFees[0];
        for ($t = 1; $t <= $maxTime; $t++) {
            foreach ($edges as $e) {
                $u = $e[0];
                $v = $e[1];
                $w = $e[2];
                if ($w > $t) continue;
                $p = $t - $w;
                if ($dp[$p][$u] !== $INF) {
                    $c = $dp[$p][$u] + $passingFees[$v];
                    if ($c < $dp[$t][$v]) $dp[$t][$v] = $c;
                }
                if ($dp[$p][$v] !== $INF) {
                    $c = $dp[$p][$v] + $passingFees[$u];
                    if ($c < $dp[$t][$u]) $dp[$t][$u] = $c;
                }
            }
        }
        $best = $INF;
        for ($t = 0; $t <= $maxTime; $t++) {
            if ($dp[$t][$n - 1] < $best) $best = $dp[$t][$n - 1];
        }
        return $best === $INF ? -1 : $best;
    }
}
```

