The minimum number of operations is target[0] plus the sum of max(0, target[i] − target[i−1]) over i ≥ 1.

Each time the target rises from one element to the next, that rise has to come from new operations that start at position i. A drop or a flat step needs no new operations, because the existing ones can simply end earlier. The first element has to be built from zero, so it contributes its full value.

Check on example 3, [3,1,5,4,2]: 3 + 0 + 4 + 0 + 0 = 7, which matches.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param Integer[] $target
     * @return Integer
     */
    function minNumberOperations($target) {
        $prev = 0;
        $res = 0;
        foreach ($target as $t) {
            if ($t > $prev) {
                $res += $t - $prev;
            }
            $prev = $t;
        }
        return $res;
    }
}
