Scan the string while tracking the number of unmatched `[`. On `[`, increment it. On `]`, decrement it if it is positive; otherwise this `]` is unmatched, so count it. Let the number of unmatched `]` be `u`. Each swap fixes two unmatched closing brackets, so the answer is `ceil(u / 2)`, which is `(u + 1) >> 1`.

Check on `]]][[[`: the three `]` are all unmatched, so `u = 3` and the answer is 2. This matches the expected output.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param String $s
     * @return Integer
     */
    function minSwaps($s) {
        $open = 0;
        $u = 0;
        $n = strlen($s);
        for ($i = 0; $i < $n; $i++) {
            if ($s[$i] === '[') {
                $open++;
            } else {
                if ($open > 0) {
                    $open--;
                } else {
                    $u++;
                }
            }
        }
        return ($u + 1) >> 1;
    }
}
```

