Use a monotonic stack of indices and iterate over the array twice (indices 0 to 2n-1, taking `i % n`).

For each position, while the stack is non-empty and the value at the top index is less than the current value, pop that index and set its answer to the current value. During the first pass (`i < n`), push the current index. The result starts filled with -1, so any element that never finds a greater value keeps -1.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param Integer[] $nums
     * @return Integer[]
     */
    function nextGreaterElements($nums) {
        $n = count($nums);
        $res = array_fill(0, $n, -1);
        $stack = [];
        for ($i = 0; $i < 2 * $n; $i++) {
            $idx = $i % $n;
            $v = $nums[$idx];
            while (!empty($stack) && $nums[end($stack)] < $v) {
                $j = array_pop($stack);
                $res[$j] = $v;
            }
            if ($i < $n) {
                $stack[] = $idx;
            }
        }
        return $res;
    }
}
```

