The approach is to loop upward from n+1 and test each number for balance. For n up to 10^6, the answer is at most 1224444 (7 digits), so the loop is short enough to run directly.

The check for a number: count each digit's occurrences, then verify that every digit d that appears has a count of exactly d. A 0 digit fails automatically, since its count would be at least 1, not 0.

The nearest balanced number above 10^6 is 1224444, so the loop ends within about 224,000 steps past 10^6. Each step costs a few digit operations, which is fast.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param Integer $n
     * @return Integer
     */
    function nextBeautifulNumber($n) {
        for ($x = $n + 1; ; $x++) {
            $cnt = array_fill(0, 10, 0);
            $t = $x;
            while ($t > 0) {
                $cnt[$t % 10]++;
                $t = intdiv($t, 10);
