For each rectangle, the largest square has side `min(l, w)`. A single pass tracks the maximum side seen so far and how many rectangles reach it. When a larger side appears, the count resets to 1. When a side equals the current maximum, the count increases by 1.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param Integer[][] $rectangles
     * @return Integer
     */
    function countGoodRectangles($rectangles) {
        $max = 0;
        $count = 0;
        foreach ($rectangles as $r) {
            $m = min($r[0], $r[1]);
            if ($m > $max) {
                $max = $m;
                $count = 1;
            } elseif ($m == $max) {
                $count++;
            }
        }
        return $count;
    }
}
```

