I use a bitmask DP over subsets of `nums`.

1. Compute the total sum. If it is not divisible by `k`, return false. Otherwise the target per subset is `target = sum / k`.
2. If any element is larger than `target`, return false.
3. Let `dp[mask]` be the sum of the chosen elements modulo `target`, or -1 if the mask is unreachable. Start with `dp[0] = 0`.
4. For each reachable mask and each element `i` not in the mask, check that `dp[mask] + nums[i] <= target`. If so, set `dp[mask | (1<<i)] = (dp[mask] + nums[i]) % target`.
5. The answer is whether `dp[full]` is reachable, where `full = (1<<n) - 1`. Since the total is `k * target`, a reachable full mask means every subset was filled exactly.

Masks are visited in increasing order, which is valid because a new mask is always larger than the one it came from. With n ≤ 16 this is at most 65536 × 16 steps.

Why the modulo form is right: while filling a subset, the running sum stays below `target`. When it reaches exactly `target`, it wraps to 0 and the next subset starts. Adding an element is only allowed if the running sum stays within `target`, so no subset overflows.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param Integer[] $nums
     * @param Integer $k
     * @return Boolean
     */
    function canPartitionKSubsets($nums, $k) {
        $n = count($nums);
        $sum = array_sum($nums);
        if ($sum % $k != 0) return false;
        $target = intdiv($sum, $k);
        foreach ($nums as $x) {
            if ($x > $target) return false;
        }
        $full = (1 << $n) - 1;
        $dp = array_fill(0, $full + 1, -1);
        $dp[0] = 0;
        for ($mask = 0; $mask <= $full; $mask++) {
            if ($dp[$mask] < 0) continue;
            for ($i = 0; $i < $n; $i++) {
                if ($mask & (1 << $i)) continue;
                $s = $dp[$mask] + $nums[$i];
                if ($s <= $target) {
                    $nm = $mask | (1 << $i);
                    if ($dp[$nm] < 0) {
                        $dp[$nm] = $s % $target;
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        return $dp[$full] == 0;
    }
}
```

