This is the classic "choose n non-adjacent slices from a circular array of 3n slices" problem, which I solve with a DP on two linear arrays.

Because the array is circular, slices 0 and m-1 are adjacent, so they can't both be picked. Run the linear DP twice, once on slices[0..m-2] and once on slices[1..m-1], and take the larger result.

For a linear array a of length L, let dp[i][j] be the best sum using the first i elements with j picks, no two adjacent:
- dp[i][j] = max(dp[i-1][j], dp[i-2][j-1] + a[i-1])

Use -infinity for invalid states. For i = 1, dp[i-2] is treated as the i = 0 row, where only j = 0 is valid with value 0.

Implementation: allocate rows 0..L, initialized so that row 0 and row 1 are 0 for j = 0 and -inf otherwise. Handle the i = 1 case directly: dp[1][0] = 0 and dp[1][1] = a[0]. Setting dp[i][0] = 0 for all i and using a helper that returns 0 for j = 0 when i < 0 keeps it simple. For i >= 2 the recurrence applies directly. For i = 1, the previous index is i-2 = -1, which I treat as the row for 0 elements (j = 0 gives 0, otherwise -inf).

Edge case: m = 1 means n = 1/3, which is impossible since m is a multiple of 3, so the smallest m is 3 and n = 1. Then the linear arrays have length 2 and we pick 1, giving the max of the elements, which is correct.

Code: n = m/3; for each array compute the dp with j up to n and return dp[L][n]. Use a large negative number such as -1e9.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param Integer[] $slices
     * @return Integer
     */
    function maxSizeSlices($slices) {
        $m = count($slices);
        $n = intdiv($m, 3);
        $a = array_slice($slices, 0, $m - 1);
        $b = array_slice($slices, 1, $m - 1);
        return max($this->calc($a, $n), $this->calc($b, $n));
    }

    function calc($a, $n) {
        $L = count($a);
        $NEG = -1000000000;
        $dp = [];
        for ($i = 0; $i <= $L; $i++) {
            $dp[$i] = array_fill(0, $n + 1, $NEG);
            $dp[$i][0] = 0;
        }
        for ($i = 1; $i <= $L; $i++) {
            for ($j = 1; $j <= $n; $j++) {
                $best = $dp[$i - 1][$j];
                if ($i >= 2) {
                    $prev = $dp[$i - 2][$j - 1];
                } else {
                    $prev = ($j - 1 == 0) ? 0 : $NEG;
                }
                if ($prev > $NEG) {
                    $cand = $prev + $a[$i - 1];
                    if ($cand > $best) $best = $cand;
                }
                $dp[$i][$j] = $best;
            }
        }
        return $dp[$L][$n];
    }
}
```

