inference_trace:
Approach: union-find. For each request, find the roots of u and v. If they are already the same, the request succeeds. Otherwise, check every restriction (x, y): if the roots of x and y are equal to the roots of u and v in either order, the request fails. If no restriction blocks it, union the two components and mark the request successful.

The cost is O(requests × restrictions × α), about 10^6 operations, which is fine.

```php
class Solution {
    private $parent = [];

    private function find($x) {
        while ($this->parent[$x] != $x) {
            $this->parent[$x] = $this->parent[$this->parent[$x]];
            $x = $this->parent[$x];
        }
        return $x;
    }

    /**
     * @param Integer $n
     * @param Integer[][] $restrictions
     * @param Integer[][] $requests
     * @return Boolean[]
     */
    function friendRequests($n, $restrictions, $requests) {
        $this->parent = range(0, $n - 1);
        $res = [];
        foreach ($requests as $r) {
            $pu = $this->find($r[0]);
            $pv = $this->find($r[1]);
            if ($pu == $pv) {
                $res[] = true;
                continue;
            }
            $ok = true;
            foreach ($restrictions as $s) {
                $px = $this->find($s[0]);
                $py = $this->find($s[1]);
                if (($px == $pu && $py == $pv) || ($px == $pv && $py == $pu)) {
                    $ok = false;
                    break;
                }
            }
            if ($ok) {
                $this->parent[$pu] = $pv;
            }
            $res[] = $ok;
        }
        return $res;
    }
}
```

