The approach is to build a map from each value to the list of its indices in the constructor. Then `pick` returns a uniformly random element from the list for `target`.

This uses O(n) extra memory and O(1) time per pick. Reservoir sampling would avoid the map, but the map is fast and simple, and the constraints are small.

```php
class Solution {
    private $map = [];

    /**
     * @param Integer[] $nums
     */
    function __construct($nums) {
        foreach ($nums as $i => $v) {
            $this->map[$v][] = $i;
        }
    }

    /**
     * @param Integer $target
     * @return Integer
     */
    function pick($target) {
        $list = $this->map[$target];
        return $list[mt_rand(0, count($list) - 1)];
    }
}
```

