Two rectangles overlap with positive area exactly when their projections overlap with positive length on both axes. That means the smaller of the two right edges must be strictly greater than the larger of the two left edges, and the same must hold for the y-axis.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param Integer[] $rec1
     * @param Integer[] $rec2
     * @return Boolean
     */
    function isRectangleOverlap($rec1, $rec2) {
        return min($rec1[2], $rec2[2]) > max($rec1[0], $rec2[0])
            && min($rec1[3], $rec2[3]) > max($rec1[1], $rec2[1]);
    }
}
```

