inference_trace:
Split each cell into 4 triangles (0 = top, 1 = right, 2 = bottom, 3 = left) and merge them with union-find.

- **Blank cell:** union all 4 triangles.
- **`/`:** union top with left (0 and 3), and right with bottom (1 and 2).
- **`\`:** union top with right (0 and 1), and bottom with left (2 and 3).
- **Neighbors:** union a cell's bottom (2) with the top (0) of the cell below, and its right (1) with the left (3) of the cell to its right.

The answer is the number of connected components.

The input strings arrive already unescaped, so a `'\'` character is read in PHP as `'\\'`. Each row has length n, so I use `strlen($grid[0])` for n.

Triangle index: `(i*n + j)*4 + k`.

```php
class Solution {
    private $p = [];

    function find($x) {
        while ($this->p[$x] != $x) {
            $this->p[$x] = $this->p[$this->p[$x]];
            $x = $this->p[$x];
        }
        return $x;
    }

    function union($a, $b) {
        $a = $this->find($a);
        $b = $this->find($b);
        if ($a != $b) {
            $this->p[$a] = $b;
            $this->cnt--;
        }
    }

    private $cnt = 0;

    /**
     * @param String[] $grid
     * @return Integer
     */
    function regionsBySlashes($grid) {
        $n = count($grid);
        $total = $n * $n * 4;
        $this->p = range(0, $total - 1);
        $this->cnt = $total;
        for ($i = 0; $i < $n; $i++) {
            for ($j = 0; $j < $n; $j++) {
                $b = ($i * $n + $j) * 4;
                $c = $grid[$i][$j];
                if ($c == ' ') {
                    $this->union($b, $b + 1);
                    $this->union($b + 1, $b + 2);
                    $this->union($b + 2, $b + 3);
                } elseif ($c == '/') {
                    $this->union($b, $b + 3);
                    $this->union($b + 1, $b + 2);
                } else {
                    $this->union($b, $b + 1);
                    $this->union($b + 2, $b + 3);
                }
                if ($i + 1 < $n) {
                    $this->union($b + 2, (($i + 1) * $n + $j) * 4);
                }
                if ($j + 1 < $n) {
                    $this->union($b + 1, ($i * $n + $j + 1) * 4 + 3);
                }
            }
        }
        return $this->cnt;
    }
}
```

