I'll use the standard DFS approach: first count how many left and right parentheses must be removed, then backtrack while avoiding duplicates.

1. Scan `s` once. For `(`, increment `open`. For `)`, if `open > 0` decrement it, otherwise increment `rr`. At the end, `open` is the number of `(` to remove (`lr`) and `rr` is the number of `)` to remove.

2. Define `dfs(index, lr, rr, current string, balance)`:
   - If `index == n`, accept the string when `lr == 0`, `rr == 0` and `balance == 0`.
   - If the character is `(`:
     - Option to remove it, if `lr > 0`, which moves on with `lr - 1`.
     - Option to keep it, which increases `balance`.
   - If the character is `)`:
     - Option to remove it, if `rr > 0`.
     - Option to keep it, only if `balance > 0`.
   - Any other character is kept.

3. Duplicates are handled by collecting results in an associative array keyed by the string. This is fine for length 25 with at most 20 parentheses. Pruning on `lr` and `rr` keeps the search small.

4. Since removals are exactly `lr + rr`, the result has the minimum number of removals. The result for `")("` is `[""]`, which the key-based set handles correctly. PHP converts numeric-string array keys to ints, so I'll cast keys back to strings on output with `array_map('strval', array_keys(...))`.

```php
class Solution {
    private $res = [];
    private $s;
    private $n;

    /**
     * @param String $s
     * @return String[]
     */
    function removeInvalidParentheses($s) {
        $this->res = [];
        $this->s = $s;
        $this->n = strlen($s);
        $open = 0;
        $rr = 0;
        for ($i = 0; $i < $this->n; $i++) {
            $c = $s[$i];
            if ($c == '(') {
                $open++;
            } elseif ($c == ')') {
                if ($open > 0) $open--;
                else $rr++;
            }
        }
        $this->dfs(0, $open, $rr, "", 0);
        return array_map('strval', array_keys($this->res));
    }

    private function dfs($i, $lr, $rr, $cur, $bal) {
        if ($bal < 0) return;
        if ($i == $this->n) {
            if ($lr == 0 && $rr == 0 && $bal == 0) {
                $this->res[$cur] = true;
            }
            return;
        }
        $c = $this->s[$i];
        if ($c == '(') {
            if ($lr > 0) $this->dfs($i + 1, $lr - 1, $rr, $cur, $bal);
            $this->dfs($i + 1, $lr, $rr, $cur . $c, $bal + 1);
        } elseif ($c == ')') {
            if ($rr > 0) $this->dfs($i + 1, $lr, $rr - 1, $cur, $bal);
            if ($bal > 0) $this->dfs($i + 1, $lr, $rr, $cur . $c, $bal - 1);
        } else {
            $this->dfs($i + 1, $lr, $rr, $cur . $c, $bal);
        }
    }
}
