Track the robot's horizontal and vertical position while scanning the string. Each `U` or `D` changes y by one, and each `L` or `R` changes x by one. The robot is back at the origin exactly when both x and y are 0. The examples contain a trailing space (`"UD "`), so the code ignores any character that is not one of the four moves.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param String $moves
     * @return Boolean
     */
    function judgeCircle($moves) {
        $x = 0;
        $y = 0;
        $n = strlen($moves);
        for ($i = 0; $i < $n; $i++) {
            $c = $moves[$i];
            if ($c === 'U') $y++;
            elseif ($c === 'D') $y--;
            elseif ($c === 'L') $x--;
            elseif ($c === 'R') $x++;
        }
        return $x === 0 && $y === 0;
    }
}
```

