I'll use memoized recursion over (i, j, len), where i is the start in s1, j is the start in s2, and len is the substring length.

For each state:
- If the two substrings are equal, return true.
- If their character counts differ, return false. This pruning is optional but cheap.
- Otherwise try every split k from 1 to len-1:
  - No swap: (i, j, k) and (i+k, j+k, len-k).
  - Swap: (i, j+len-k, k) and (i+k, j, len-k).

The memo is a flat array keyed by `i*900 + j*30 + len`. With n ≤ 30 this is at most about 27,000 states, each trying up to 29 splits, so it runs well within limits.

I use a private helper method, which is fine because the required `isScramble` signature is unchanged. The memo and strings are stored as instance properties.

```php
class Solution {
    private $a;
    private $b;
    private $memo = [];

    /**
     * @param String $s1
     * @param String $s2
     * @return Boolean
     */
    function isScramble($s1, $s2) {
        $this->a = $s1;
        $this->b = $s2;
        $this->memo = [];
        $n = strlen($s1);
        if ($n != strlen($s2)) return false;
        return $this->go(0, 0, $n);
    }

    private function go($i, $j, $len) {
        $key = $i * 900 + $j * 30 + $len;
        if (isset($this->memo[$key])) return $this->memo[$key];
        $x = substr($this->a, $i, $len);
        $y = substr($this->b, $j, $len);
        if ($x === $y) return $this->memo[$key] = true;
        if ($len == 1) return $this->memo[$key] = false;
        $cnt = array_fill(0, 26, 0);
        for ($t = 0; $t < $len; $t++) {
            $cnt[ord($x[$t]) - 97]++;
            $cnt[ord($y[$t]) - 97]--;
        }
        foreach ($cnt as $c) {
            if ($c != 0) return $this->memo[$key] = false;
        }
        for ($k = 1; $k < $len; $k++) {
            if ($this->go($i, $j, $k) && $this->go($i + $k, $j + $k, $len - $k)) {
                return $this->memo[$key] = true;
            }
            if ($this->go($i, $j + $len - $k, $k) && $this->go($i + $k, $j, $len - $k)) {
                return $this->memo[$key] = true;
            }
        }
        return $this->memo[$key] = false;
    }
}
