inference_trace:
Walk the spiral directly. The step lengths follow the pattern 1, 1, 2, 2, 3, 3, ..., with directions east, south, west, north repeating.

1. Start at `(rStart, cStart)` and record it, since the start is always inside the grid.
2. For each leg, move one cell at a time in the current direction. After each move, record the cell if it lies inside the grid.
3. After every leg, turn clockwise. After every second leg, increase the step length by 1.
4. Stop once `rows * cols` cells have been recorded.

The loop is bounded because the spiral eventually covers the whole grid.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param Integer $rows
     * @param Integer $cols
     * @param Integer $rStart
     * @param Integer $cStart
     * @return Integer[][]
     */
    function spiralMatrixIII($rows, $cols, $rStart, $cStart) {
        $res = [[$rStart, $cStart]];
        $total = $rows * $cols;
        $dr = [0, 1, 0, -1];
        $dc = [1, 0, -1, 0];
        $r = $rStart;
        $c = $cStart;
        $d = 0;
        $len = 1;
        while (count($res) < $total) {
            for ($t = 0; $t < 2; $t++) {
                for ($i = 0; $i < $len; $i++) {
                    $r += $dr[$d];
                    $c += $dc[$d];
                    if ($r >= 0 && $r < $rows && $c >= 0 && $c < $cols) {
                        $res[] = [$r, $c];
                    }
                }
                $d = ($d + 1) % 4;
            }
            $len++;
        }
        return $res;
    }
}
```

