inference_trace:
This is a bitmask DP over the letters of the target. The state is the set of target positions already covered, and `dp[mask]` is the fewest stickers needed to cover that set.

Preprocessing:
1. Compute a letter-count array for each sticker.
2. Drop any sticker that has no letter in common with the target. (The examples show trailing spaces in the words. Those would be stripped, and the constraints say only lowercase letters appear anyway.)

Transitions:
1. Start with `dp[0] = 0` and every other state unreached.
2. For each reached mask, take the lowest unset bit `i`. Some sticker must cover that position, so only stickers containing `target[i]` need to be tried.
3. For each such sticker, copy its counts and walk through the target positions `j`. If `j` is not in the mask and the sticker still has a letter `target[j]`, set bit `j` in the new mask and decrement that count.
4. Update `dp[newmask] = min(dp[newmask], dp[mask] + 1)`.

Because `newmask` is a strict superset of `mask` (it includes bit `i`), it is always numerically larger. Processing masks in increasing order is therefore valid.

The answer is `dp[full]`, or `-1` if that state is unreachable.

Cost: there are 2^15 = 32768 masks, up to 50 stickers, and 15 positions per sticker, about 25M operations. That is acceptable.

To speed this up, I pre-filter the stickers per target letter. `byLetter[c]` holds the indices of stickers containing letter `c`.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param String[] $stickers
     * @param String $target
     * @return Integer
     */
    function minStickers($stickers, $target) {
        $target = trim($target);
        $n = strlen($target);
        $counts = [];
        $byLetter = [];
        foreach ($stickers as $s) {
            $s = trim($s);
            $c = array_fill(0, 26, 0);
            for ($i = 0; $i < strlen($s); $i++) {
                $c[ord($s[$i]) - 97]++;
            }
            $idx = count($counts);
            $counts[] = $c;
            for ($k = 0; $k < 26; $k++) {
                if ($c[$k] > 0) $byLetter[$k][] = $idx;
            }
        }
        $full = (1 << $n) - 1;
        $INF = 1000000;
        $dp = array_fill(0, $full + 1, $INF);
        $dp[0] = 0;
        $t = [];
        for ($i = 0; $i < $n; $i++) $t[$i] = ord($target[$i]) - 97;
        for ($mask = 0; $mask < $full; $mask++) {
            if ($dp[$mask] >= $INF) continue;
            $i = 0;
            while ($mask & (1 << $i)) $i++;
            if (!isset($byLetter[$t[$i]])) continue;
            foreach ($byLetter[$t[$i]] as $si) {
                $c = $counts[$si];
                $nm = $mask;
                for ($j = 0; $j < $n; $j++) {
                    if (!($nm & (1 << $j)) && $c[$t[$j]] > 0) {
                        $c[$t[$j]]--;
                        $nm |= (1 << $j);
                    }
                }
                if ($dp[$mask] + 1 < $dp[$nm]) $dp[$nm] = $dp[$mask] + 1;
            }
        }
        return $dp[$full] >= $INF ? -1 : $dp[$full];
    }
}
```

