Approach: build a trie of the reversed words, and keep the stream as a list of characters. On each query, walk the trie from the newest character backwards, returning true as soon as a node marks the end of a word. The walk stops at the longest word length (at most 200), so each query is cheap.

The examples show words with trailing spaces (e.g. "cd "), which look like formatting artifacts. The constraints say words are lowercase letters only, so I'll use the strings as given. If a trailing space were really part of a word, it would be inserted into the trie like any other character. The query letters carry the same artifact, so the two stay consistent either way.

Implementation details:
- The trie is stored as arrays: `$this->next[node][char]` gives the child, and `$this->end[node]` marks a word end.
- Stream characters go into an array `$this->s`, and I track `$this->maxLen`.
- In `query`, append the letter, then start at the root with `i = count - 1` and step back at most `maxLen` characters. If a child is missing, return false. If the child is a word end, return true.

```php
class StreamChecker {
    private $next = [];
    private $end = [];
    private $s = [];
    private $maxLen = 0;

    /**
     * @param String[] $words
     */
    function __construct($words) {
        $this->next = [[]];
        $this->end = [false];
        foreach ($words as $w) {
            $len = strlen($w);
            if ($len > $this->maxLen) $this->maxLen = $len;
            $node = 0;
            for ($i = $len - 1; $i >= 0; $i--) {
                $c = $w[$i];
                if (!isset($this->next[$node][$c])) {
                    $this->next[] = [];
                    $this->end[] = false;
                    $this->next[$node][$c] = count($this->next) - 1;
                }
                $node = $this->next[$node][$c];
            }
            $this->end[$node] = true;
        }
    }

    /**
     * @param String $letter
     * @return Boolean
     */
    function query($letter) {
        $this->s[] = $letter;
        $node = 0;
        $n = count($this->s);
        $lim = max(0, $n - $this->maxLen);
        for ($i = $n - 1; $i >= $lim; $i--) {
            $c = $this->s[$i];
            if (!isset($this->next[$node][$c])) return false;
            $node = $this->next[$node][$c];
            if ($this->end[$node]) return true;
        }
        return false;
    }
}
```

