inference_trace:
Count the soldiers in each row, sort the rows by (count, index), and return the first k indices. The count can be a plain sum of the row, since the matrix only contains 0s and 1s. Encoding each row as `count * 1000 + index` lets a single integer sort handle both the count and the tie-break by index. The index is at most 99, so 1000 is a safe multiplier. The index is then recovered with `% 1000`.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param Integer[][] $mat
     * @param Integer $k
     * @return Integer[]
     */
    function kWeakestRows($mat, $k) {
        $keys = [];
        foreach ($mat as $i => $row) {
            $keys[] = array_sum($row) * 1000 + $i;
        }
        sort($keys);
        $res = [];
        for ($j = 0; $j < $k; $j++) {
            $res[] = $keys[$j] % 1000;
        }
        return $res;
    }
}
```

