inference_trace:
A word is uncommon exactly when it appears once in the combined text of both sentences. So I count every word across `s1` and `s2` together and return the words whose count is 1.

One PHP detail: array keys that look like integers get cast to ints, but the words here are only lowercase letters, so that cannot happen.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param String $s1
     * @param String $s2
     * @return String[]
     */
    function uncommonFromSentences($s1, $s2) {
        $counts = [];
        foreach (explode(' ', $s1 . ' ' . $s2) as $w) {
            if ($w === '') continue;
            if (!isset($counts[$w])) $counts[$w] = 0;
            $counts[$w]++;
        }
        $res = [];
        foreach ($counts as $w => $c) {
            if ($c == 1) $res[] = (string)$w;
        }
        return $res;
    }
}
```

