This is a shortest-path problem on words, so I use BFS. To find neighbours quickly, I group words by wildcard pattern: for each word, replace position i with `*` to get a pattern such as `h*t`. Words that share a pattern differ by exactly one letter.

Steps:
1. Put every word of `wordList` into a set. If `endWord` is not in the set, return 0.
2. Build a map from each pattern to the list of words that produce it.
3. Run BFS from `beginWord` with distance 1, keeping a visited set.
4. For each dequeued word and each position, look up its pattern. Each unvisited word under that pattern is enqueued with distance + 1. If that word is `endWord`, return its distance.
5. Clear a pattern's list after it has been used so it is not scanned again.
6. If the queue empties without reaching `endWord`, return 0.

I use an array with an index pointer as the queue. Each entry is a `[word, distance]` pair.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param String $beginWord
     * @param String $endWord
     * @param String[] $wordList
     * @return Integer
     */
    function ladderLength($beginWord, $endWord, $wordList) {
        $set = array_flip($wordList);
        if (!isset($set[$endWord])) return 0;
        $map = [];
        foreach ($wordList as $w) {
            $len = strlen($w);
            for ($i = 0; $i < $len; $i++) {
                $p = substr($w, 0, $i) . '*' . substr($w, $i + 1);
                $map[$p][] = $w;
            }
        }
        $visited = [$beginWord => true];
        $queue = [[$beginWord, 1]];
        $head = 0;
        while ($head < count($queue)) {
            [$w, $d] = $queue[$head++];
            $len = strlen($w);
            for ($i = 0; $i < $len; $i++) {
                $p = substr($w, 0, $i) . '*' . substr($w, $i + 1);
                if (!isset($map[$p])) continue;
                foreach ($map[$p] as $n) {
                    if ($n === $endWord) return $d + 1;
                    if (!isset($visited[$n])) {
                        $visited[$n] = true;
                        $queue[] = [$n, $d + 1];
                    }
                }
                unset($map[$p]);
            }
        }
        return 0;
    }
}
```

